{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1792758003358704583,"compiled_state":{"alias":"ominous-lineny-salmon","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"8552a6d6444f194fa4075bf1e404ac788bd6e756836a4522652193cfde07d6d5","event_uuid":"a61a6b31-cf1d-430c-98f5-062f7d76c94e","position":{"commit_sha":"3aa4762a683dc7257ed957c6e0fbaa6f08cf864c","position":"1792738973169234560-a61a6b31-cf1d-430c-98f5-062f7d76c94e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"4d21ad7ffde02246cbd2c72d780b46b2a039945f4b24d5e532c956cbcbce705f","event_uuid":"923fc7d3-1517-42e1-8b50-53d38b3a28a9","position":{"commit_sha":"67710d79184190e571c9671c4e9ac67db3f9ef64","position":"1792738982309249329-923fc7d3-1517-42e1-8b50-53d38b3a28a9"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1792738973169234560,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"923fc7d3-1517-42e1-8b50-53d38b3a28a9","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"c115-1b25-6884-4f9c"}],"description":"## Observation\nIn tests/unit/reconciler/orchestrate/test_mode_cap_enforcement.py, test_spot_check_sampling_is_deterministic_across_runs calls _fresh_renderer() twice. That helper calls importlib.import_module(\"rebar.reconciler.manifest_renderer\") with the same name in one Python process, so both calls return the cached module. The test then calls render_throttle twice and compares the nonempty spot_check keys. Its helper comment and assertion describe fresh module loads and per-process Python hash randomization, but the test never starts another process or changes PYTHONHASHSEED. This was found during the comment-remediation review of intangible-corruptful-numbat; the prose-only patch must leave this unlisted helper/assertion unchanged.\n\n## Plan\nCreate a controlled cross-process regression check that renders the same mutation fixture under at least 2 explicit distinct PYTHONHASHSEED values, captures the selected spot-check keys, and asserts the same nonempty selection. Keep the test hermetic and preserve the existing in-process assertion as useful separate coverage if desired. Correct the helper/comment/assertion to describe what each check proves.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- Given the same 200-mutation fixture and 2 distinct PYTHONHASHSEED values, when independent Python processes render the spot-check selection, then they return the same nonempty ordered keys.\n- Given the existing in-process check, when it runs, then its comment and assertion describe only the behavior it actually observes.\n- Focused mode-cap tests and make verify pass after the test change.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":["rebar"],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["test-quality"],"ticket_id":"f154-507e-1162-4c9e","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Make spot-check determinism test exercise distinct hash seeds","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["a61a6b31-cf1d-430c-98f5-062f7d76c94e","923fc7d3-1517-42e1-8b50-53d38b3a28a9"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1792758003358704583,"uuid":"c7ed7f41-bc80-43ac-9091-7095eb064bee"}